# Frontend Architecture Rule

## Layering
- Route composition stays in `frontend/app/*`.
- Shared visual primitives belong in `frontend/components/ui/*`.
- Reusable layout scaffolding belongs in `frontend/components/layout/*`.
- Shared helpers belong in `frontend/lib/*`.

## Reuse and Naming
- Use PascalCase component names and kebab-case filenames.
- Prefer adding variants to existing primitives over creating near-duplicate components.
- Keep public component APIs small and composable.

## Styling Strategy
- Tailwind utilities remain the primary styling mechanism.
- Semantic tokens from global CSS are the source of truth.
- Avoid copy-pasting long class strings across routes when a shared primitive or helper can absorb them.

## Change Safety
- Preserve existing route behavior and external link behavior during visual refactors.
- Refactors should be incremental: primitives first, route migration second.
